{"text": "Page 1of3\nCORESTA CO SUB-COMMITTEE,\n\nFrankfurt, May 3, 2000\n3. meeting.\nList of participants\n\u2018British American Tobacco Tirgen Hollweg\n\u2018Borgwaldt Bruno Kiuss\nKatrin Schade\nFiltrona Jeremy Smith\n\u201cHouse of Prince Hans V. Thomsen\nImperial (Colin Fill\n\u2018Japan Tobacco \u2018Shizuo Suhara\nIL. Tiedemanns Rolf Aa. Olsen\nPhilip Morris. \u2018Dimiri Parthenopoulos\nReemisma Henning Lutz\nRJ. Reynolds \u2018Linda Crumpler\nRJ. Reynolds Intemational Ferdi Krull\n\nApologies from: Yves Saint Jalm (Seita) and Joaquin Serabia.\n\nHVT distributed minutes from 2. meeting and received comments which are incorporated in an\nedited version.\n\nBorgwaldt reported on a new design of the cover plate with changed hole pattern. Had tested\ndifferent position of holes. Holes close to the outer periphery ofthe plated resulted in a very\n\u2018unstable (immeasurable) airflow. The design remains to be optimised (hole size, position and\norm). Results till now confirm that holes close to the centre results in a stable airflow. See\nattachment 1 for smoking results of 5 cigarettes)\n\nBorgwaldt had tested airflow probes of different design and found results from omni directional and\nbi-directional probes to be equal.\n\nCO measurement using extemal or in-built apparatus gave same results, but the calibration rust be\nperformed very precisely to avoid apparent differences,\n\nPParthenopoulos reported on smoking of the CM3 and an internal monitor with the Borwaldt plate\nwiththe inner 3 holes open. The results in attachment 2 are based on smoking of 3 cigarettes with\nthe modified plate ~ the reference results are means over 1 month, Though the results are \u201cinitial\u201d\nthey look encouraging.\n\n\u2018Borgwaldt points to the need for a plate that is transparent ~ itis not practical thatthe operator\n\u2018cannot see the cigarettes during smoking. This must also be remembered in relation to RM20. There\nis also a need for smoking results from cigarettes with a CO yield about 10 mg to investigate the\neffect close to the possible future CO-ceiling, We need results from a series of commercial brands.\n\nHollweg pointed to the fact that not only temperature was an important parameter \u2014 the diffusion\n\ncoefficient of CO from the centre ofthe cigarette to is periphery is important and depends on the CO\nconcentration of CO outside the cigarette,\n\n\u2018CORESTA CO Sub Commitee Hans Valdemar Thomsen 05.09.00\n\nepgssrze0z", "words": [{"text": "Page", "x0": 556, "y0": 112, "x1": 577, "y1": 123, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "1of3", "x0": 584, "y0": 112, "x1": 607, "y1": 121, "conf": 53.0}, {"text": "CORESTA", "x0": 249, "y0": 137, "x1": 311, "y1": 147, "conf": 79.0}, {"text": "CO", "x0": 314, "y0": 137, "x1": 333, "y1": 147, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "SUB-COMMITTEE,", "x0": 336, "y0": 137, "x1": 449, "y1": 147, "conf": 60.0}, {"text": "Frankfurt,", "x0": 285, "y0": 152, "x1": 343, "y1": 165, "conf": 83.0}, {"text": "May", "x0": 346, "y0": 152, "x1": 371, "y1": 165, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "3,", "x0": 374, "y0": 152, "x1": 384, "y1": 164, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "2000", "x0": 387, "y0": 152, "x1": 413, "y1": 162, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "3.", "x0": 320, "y0": 168, "x1": 330, "y1": 178, "conf": 70.0}, {"text": "meeting.", "x0": 334, "y0": 168, "x1": 377, "y1": 181, "conf": 57.0}, {"text": "List", "x0": 90, "y0": 199, "x1": 112, "y1": 209, "conf": 50.0}, {"text": "of", "x0": 115, "y0": 190, "x1": 125, "y1": 219, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "participants", "x0": 129, "y0": 199, "x1": 196, "y1": 212, "conf": 32.0}, {"text": "\u2018British", "x0": 166, "y0": 215, "x1": 202, "y1": 225, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "American", "x0": 205, "y0": 216, "x1": 256, "y1": 226, "conf": 86.0}, {"text": "Tobacco", "x0": 259, "y0": 216, "x1": 303, "y1": 225, "conf": 77.0}, {"text": "Tirgen", "x0": 402, "y0": 215, "x1": 436, "y1": 229, "conf": 24.0}, {"text": "Hollweg", "x0": 440, "y0": 215, "x1": 489, "y1": 229, "conf": 35.0}, {"text": "\u2018Bor